 # recordload
-Go 1.22 library. Load reads key=value records in order. Blank lines are ignored.
-The current task adds comment lines beginning with # and reports malformed records
-using an exported *LineError with Line (one-based physical line) and Text fields.
-Load returns the valid prefix on malformed input or read failure. The caller's
-reader errors remain inspectable. Process bytes returned alongside a read error;
-EOF is normal completion. Successful errors are nil interfaces. No line-size cap
-is promised. Empty keys and values are accepted. Readers are borrowed.
+
+Go 1.22 library. `Load` reads `key=value` records in order. Blank lines and lines
+whose first character is `#` are ignored. Keys and values may be empty; the first
+`=` separates them.
+
+Malformed records return a `*LineError` with the one-based physical line number
+and original line text. `Load` also returns all records parsed before malformed
+input or a reader failure. Reader failures wrap the original error, so callers
+can inspect it with `errors.Is` or `errors.As`. Bytes returned together with a
+reader error are processed before the error is returned. `io.EOF` means normal
+completion, including when it accompanies the final bytes.
+
+Readers are borrowed and are not closed. There is no promised line-size limit.
